  "sourceSolutions": [
    {
      "source": "1103",
      "task": "Construct all three real-function graphs with correct domains, branches and omitted points.",
      "functions": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "function": "y=1/|x|",
          "domain": "Real x!=0.",
          "solution": "For x<0,y=-1/x>0;for x>0,y=1/x>0. The graph is even,with two positive branches symmetric about the y-axis. It increases toward positive infinity on the left as x approaches0-,and decreases from positive infinity on the right as x increases from0+. Vertical asymptote x=0,horizontal asymptote y=0;neither axis is met. Sample points(-2,1/2),(-1,1),(1,1),(2,1/2). No value or filled point atx=0."
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "function": "y=1/sqrt(x)",
          "domain": "Real x>0;the square-root condition x>=0 is strengthened by the nonzero denominator.",
          "solution": "Only the first-quadrant branch exists. It is positive and strictly decreasing,with y approaching infinity as x approaches0+ and approaching0 as x approaches positive infinity. Asymptotesx0,y0;no point atzero,no negative-x branch. Sample points(1/4,2),(1,1),(4,1/2)."
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "function": "y=x^3/|x|",
          "domain": "Real x!=0,retained after simplification.",
          "solution": "Forx<0,|x|=-x andy=-x^2;forx>0,y=x^2. Thus it is the increasing odd graph ofx|x| with the origin omitted,not an everywhere-defined polynomial. Left branch is in the third quadrant,right in the first,both approach(0,0) without including it. Show an open hole at the origin. Sample points(-2,-4),(-1,-1),(1,1),(2,4)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "1104",
      "task": "Construct all four graphs,using sqrt(x^2)=|x| with sign cases and horizontal shifts.",
      "functions": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "function": "y=sqrt(x^2)+x",
          "domain": "All real x.",
          "solution": "y=|x|+x equals0 forx<=0 and2x forx>=0. The included vertex is(0,0),with a left horizontal ray on the x-axis and right ray of slope2. No hole. Sample(-2,0),(-1,0),(0,0),(1,2),(2,4)."
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "function": "y=sqrt(x^2)-x",
          "domain": "All real x.",
          "solution": "y=|x|-x equals-2x forx<=0 and0 forx>=0. Included vertex(0,0),left ray of slope-2 and right horizontal ray on the x-axis. Sample(-2,4),(-1,2),(0,0),(1,0),(2,0)."
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "function": "y=|x+2|",
          "domain": "All real x.",
          "solution": "V-shaped graph with included vertex(-2,0). Left rayy=-x-2 forx<=-2,slope-1;right rayy=x+2 forx>=-2,slope1. Sample(-3,1),(-2,0),(-1,1),(0,2). Range nonnegative;the shift is left2,not up2 or right2."
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "function": "y=|x-1|",
          "domain": "All real x.",
          "solution": "V-shaped graph with included vertex(1,0). Left rayy=1-x forx<=1,slope-1;right rayy=x-1 forx>=1,slope1. Sample(0,1),(1,0),(2,1),(3,2). Range nonnegative;the shift is right1,not down1 or left1."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "1105",
      "task": "Construct the full two-branch graph,with domain,turning points and asymptotic directions.",
      "function": "y=x+1/x",
      "domain": "Real x!=0.",
      "solution": "The function is odd. Forx>0,x+1/x-2=(x-1)^2/x>=0,with minimum(1,2);forx<0 it is<=-2,with maximum(-1,-2). Thus no real zero or intersection with either axis. Vertical asymptotex0,oblique asymptotey=x sincey-x=1/x tends0 at either infinite end. Right branch decreases from positive infinity to(1,2),then increases;left branch increases to(-1,-2),then decreases to negative infinity asx approaches0-. Sample points(-2,-5/2),(-1,-2),(-1/2,-5/2),(1/2,5/2),(1,2),(2,5/2). The liney=x is a guide/asymptote,not a component of the graph;do not join branches acrossx=0."
    }
  ],
